cggames
=======

Games for CGTK, ported from the GNOME 1 games (gnome-games 1.4.0.4) as
plain CGTK programs, with nothing of GNOME left in them, and new ones
written the same way.

  cgchess     Chess against GNU Chess or Stockfish, new
  cgfreecell  FreeCell, from GNOME Freecell
  cghanafuda  Flower card games, new: Koi-Koi and Oicho-Kabu
  cghearts    Hearts card game against the computer, new
  cgmahjong   Tile matching game, from GNOME Mahjongg
  cgminesweep Minefield game, from GNOME Mines
  cgsolitaire Classic Solitaire

Each game keeps its settings in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cggames/GAME.conf
and its best scores in $XDG_DATA_HOME/cggames/GAME.scores
(~/.config and ~/.local/share by default).

Building
--------

It needs CGTK 1.4, and autoconf and automake to build
from git; cgchess wants GNU Chess (gnuchess) or Stockfish (stockfish),
to play against, or any UCI chess engine:

  autoreconf -vif
  ./configure
  make
  make install

Translations
------------

The games share one text domain, cggames, with its catalogues in po:
Chinese (simplified), French, German, Japanese, Portuguese (Brazil),
Russian and Spanish. The desktop files carry the same languages. They
were machine translated and have not been reviewed by native speakers.

History
-------

cgfreecell, cgmahjong and cgminesweep come from GNOME Freecell, GNOME
Mahjongg and GNOME Mines of gnome-games 1.4.0.4. The ChangeLogs that
Mahjongg and Mines had when they were brought in are in history/,
unchanged.

Licence
-------

The games are under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later
(COPYING), as gnome-games was.

The playing cards, common/cards/deck.svg, are a public domain deck
from Wikimedia Commons:
https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Public_domain_complete_playing_card_deck.svg
The card backs in common/cards/backs were drawn for these games, and
are under the GPL with the rest.

The mahjong tiles' faces, cgmahjong/tiles/tiles.svg, are public domain
(CC0) riichi tiles, from
https://github.com/FluffyStuff/riichi-mahjong-tiles, put in one picture
with what CGTK can't draw taken out. The flowers and seasons were
drawn for these games, and are under the GPL with the rest.

The flower cards, cghanafuda/cards/*.svg, were drawn for these games,
and are under the GPL with the rest: traditional.svg with black leaves,
and light.svg the same cards with green leaves and brown wood.

The chess pieces, cgchess/pieces/*.svg, are under the GPL, version 2
or later: cburnett.svg is Colin M. L. Burnett's set, and merida.svg
Armando Hernandez Marroquin's Merida, both as lichess.org has them
(https://github.com/lichess-org/lila), each set's twelve pieces put in
one picture here.

The games' icons were drawn for them, and are under the GPL with the
rest. Each is one picture, as cgchess/icons/cgchess.svg, with the sizes
of it and the XPM that common/render-icons.sh makes kept beside it.
Three have a part of the pictures above in them: the knight in
cgchess's is Merida's, the king in cgfreecell's is the deck's king of
spades, and the red dragon on the tile in cgmahjong's is the riichi
tiles'.

The mahjong maps after Easy, cgmahjong/layouts.map, are GNOME
Mahjongg's from gnome-games 2.32.1, under the GPL as gnome-games was.
